# Shell scripts must stay LF, even when a checkout has core.autocrlf=true (a
# common Windows/WSL default). Otherwise git rewrites them to CRLF, which gives
# a broken shebang (`/bin/bash\r`: No such file or directory) and `$'\r'` errors
# in any script that sources another. eol=lf overrides autocrlf per file.
*.sh text eol=lf
